From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:31:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gmain: reap children with waitpid() when waitid() has no
 P_PIDFD

g_child_watch_source_new() watches a child through pidfd_open() when that
works, and g_child_watch_dispatch() then collects it with
waitid(P_PIDFD, ...). waitid() only learned P_PIDFD in Linux 5.4, but
Android's older kernels backport pidfd_open() for lmkd, so on those the
pidfd is created and polls fine and only waitid() fails, with EINVAL.

The dispatch then assumed the child was gone, called the watch with -1
as its status and never reaped it. On a Titan Pocket (4.14) every service
ls-hubd started on demand and every child LunaSysService ran stayed a
zombie for the life of the system, each with a "waitid(...) failed:
Invalid argument (22)" warning.

On EINVAL, fall through to the waitpid() path the non-pidfd case already
uses, which reaps the child and reports its real status. Other errors
keep their warning and old handling.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 glib/gmain.c | 25 +++++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/glib/gmain.c
+++ b/glib/gmain.c
@@ -6139,12 +6139,25 @@ g_child_watch_dispatch (GSource    *source,
           {
             int errsv = errno;
 
-            g_warning (G_STRLOC ": waitid(pid:%" G_PID_FORMAT ", pidfd=%d) failed: %s (%d). %s",
-                       child_watch_source->pid, child_watch_source->poll.fd, g_strerror (errsv), errsv,
-                       "See documentation of g_child_watch_source_new() for possible causes.");
+            if (errsv == EINVAL)
+              {
+                /* waitid() has no P_PIDFD before Linux 5.4, but Android
+                 * kernels older than that backport pidfd_open() (for lmkd),
+                 * so the pidfd above works and only this fails. Reap with
+                 * waitpid() below instead: assuming the child is gone left
+                 * it a zombie and reported -1 as its status. */
+                g_debug (G_STRLOC ": waitid(P_PIDFD) is not supported, reaping pid %" G_PID_FORMAT " with waitpid()",
+                         child_watch_source->pid);
+              }
+            else
+              {
+                g_warning (G_STRLOC ": waitid(pid:%" G_PID_FORMAT ", pidfd=%d) failed: %s (%d). %s",
+                           child_watch_source->pid, child_watch_source->poll.fd, g_strerror (errsv), errsv,
+                           "See documentation of g_child_watch_source_new() for possible causes.");
 
-            /* Assume the process is gone and proceed. */
-            child_exited = TRUE;
+                /* Assume the process is gone and proceed. */
+                child_exited = TRUE;
+              }
           }
       }
 #endif /* HAVE_PIDFD*/
